WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:03.003
I'm going to start boxing up my books

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:08.508
and my heart really hurts.

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:08.942
A Florida

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.076
elementary school teacher

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:11.611
says she removed the books

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.146
from her classroom library

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:15.215
to comply with the new state law.

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.550
I decided to remove the books

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.853
from my classroom library

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:20.854
out of necessity.

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:22.355
It wasn't really a choice.

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:24.591
Our district gave us an initiative.

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:26.760
So districts are scrambling

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.928
to try and keep up with this legislation.

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.263
They're already

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:31.865
understaffed, underfunded,

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:32.999
and it's

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.200
causing a lot of chaos

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.035
within the district.

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:37.170
So my particular district was

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.173
they decided to have teachers

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:41.341
remove access

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:42.976
to all classroom libraries

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:44.677
and media centers

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.713
until all books could be vetted.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:48.081
Duval County

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:49.282
Public Schools has directed

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:51.451
teachers to use only approved books,

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:52.585
while Media Center

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:53.219
and classroom

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.621
library books are reviewed by

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:56.122
a certified media specialist.

00:00:57.524 --> 00:01:00.226
My students were extremely upset

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.861
and they,

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:02.162
you know,

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:03.530
the first thing they did, they walked in

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:04.731
and they looked to the corner

00:01:04.731 --> 00:01:05.632
where our little free

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:06.933
library is that we keep

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:07.801
and they just said,

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.402
where are our books at?

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:10.703
What did you do with our books?

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:12.372
Are you are you moving the library?

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:13.273
What's happening?

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:14.841
School districts across the state

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:16.509
are implementing a contentious law.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:17.610
Republican Governor Ron

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.512
DeSantis signed last summer.

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.147
It's all part of his push to legislate

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:23.216
what is taught in Florida classrooms,

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:23.950
including topics

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:26.119
related to race and sexual orientation.

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:28.321
HB 1467 calls

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:30.323
for, quote, curriculum transparency

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:30.990
and says

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.292
all library materials

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:34.394
should be, quote, free of pornography.

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:35.829
It also requires

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:37.230
that books be vetted by a media

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.932
specialist certified by the state

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:42.602
video showing empty library

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:43.770
shelves went viral.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:44.737
But a Duval district

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:45.538
spokesman said

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:46.506
it didn't show, quote,

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:48.208
the other side of the library

00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:50.743
fully stocked and open to students

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:52.378
I'm shocked and I'm confused.

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:54.514
And there's so much political posturing

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:57.884
and there's so much confusion.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.853
I truly feel in my heart

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:00.653
like public schools

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:02.255
are being set up to fail.

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:03.156
A Duval spokesman

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:04.357
says during the book review

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:05.191
period, quote,

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:06.292
There should not be a case

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:08.428
when a classroom doesn't have any books.

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:09.963
And that, quote, the list of approved

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:11.264
books grows every day.

